<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-alto</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to raise</i>, <i>exalt</i> (post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inaltata est cava mundi rotunditas in modum
					sphaerae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Trism. p. 85, 41</span></i>
			 dub. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui superbos deprimit, humiles inaltat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Paul. Carm. 21, 738</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
